!
! How far an input has come toward its threshold, in hundredths of a
! percent, held at 10000, in Trebago (talisman_rules.h TL1). Trebago is
! exact and has no floor, so the floor is counted: of the steps k = 1 to
! 10000, those with k * need <= 10000 * have, each counted as
! min(1, max(0, 10000 * have - k * need + 1)), which is 1 or 0 for
! integers. That is min(10000, floor(10000 * have / need)) for any need
! above 0. Trebago takes every integer, where Sutra refuses a need of 0, a
! negative, or one past 9(9): there the two disagree and it is held.
trebago reach
  in  have(n), need(n)
  out reach(n)
  reach(i) = sum(k = 1:10000, min(1, max(0, 10000 * have(i) - k * need(i) + 1)))
end
